</section>

<!-- how it works -->
<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head center reveal">
      <span class="kicker">set up in 2 minutes</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">How it works</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal">
        <h3>Install on your computer</h3>
        <p>On a <b>Mac</b>, download the Pounce desktop app. On <b>Windows or Linux</b>, run the headless Bridge. Prefer a terminal? <b class="mono">npx use-pounce</b> does it in one line. Every path starts your agent host and shows a QR.</p>
        <svg class="wire" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M3 11h13m0 0-4-4m4 4-4 4"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal">
        <h3>Scan the QR</h3>
        <p>Open Pounce on your phone, tap Sync, and point the camera at the code in the desktop app (or your terminal). That's the whole setup.</p>
        <svg class="wire" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M3 11h13m0 0-4-4m4 4-4 4"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal">
        <h3>Pounce from anywhere</h3>
        <p>Your sessions sync instantly. Steer agents, reply, review diffs, and ship — one-handed, from the couch or the commute.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:34px">
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/how-it-works" style="display:inline-flex">
        <span class="t"><span>See the full walkthrough →</span></span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- analytics -->
<section id="analytics">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="kicker">know what you're spending</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Every token, accounted for</h2>
      <p class="sec-lead">Pounce reads the usage your agents already write to disk — no extra instrumentation, nothing sent anywhere. Tokens, spend, sessions and messages across every machine and every agent, from a week to a year.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="analytics">
      <figure class="an-shot reveal">
        <div class="device"><img src="/assets/shot-activity.png" alt="Pounce Activity screen — tokens, estimated spend, sessions and messages across every agent, with a contribution heatmap and per-plan usage" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </figure>
      <div class="an-copy">
        <div class="an-item reveal">
          <h3>The number your agent reports</h3>
          <p>Token counts come straight from each agent's own records, so they match the figure on your Claude or Codex account page. The cached share sits beside the total — most of a long session is context re-read from cache, and that's cheap, not waste.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="an-item reveal">
          <h3>Tap any figure to open it up</h3>
          <p>Every stat opens onto its own page: a week/month/year trend, then a breakdown by agent, by model, and by project. That's where you find the model quietly costing more than the bigger one next to it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="an-item reveal">
          <h3>Plan usage, not guesswork</h3>
          <p>On a subscription the marginal cost of a turn is zero, so Pounce shows how much of each rolling rate-limit window you've burned and when it resets. Dollar figures are labelled list price — never passed off as a bill.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

